<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<h1 class="title mb-12">About</h1>
	<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus max-w-none">
		<p>
			I’m Manveer Singh Tib, a junior at Wakeland High School in Frisco, TX. I’m aiming toward
			biomedical engineering, and along the way I’ve picked up chess (1700 ELO), robotics, and a
			habit of building AI tools for problems I think deserve more attention than they get.
		</p>
		<p>
			The thread running through most of what I build is access: the tools to diagnose and treat
			disease usually exist somewhere, but they don’t always reach the people who need them. That’s
			the problem I keep coming back to, in my ISM research and in the platforms I build on the
			side.
		</p>

		<h2>Portfolio Introduction</h2>
		<VideoEmbed id="sXygqC4kCRs" title="Portfolio Introduction, Manveer Singh Tib" />

		<h2>Independent Study &#38; Mentorship (ISM)</h2>
		<p>
			ISM is a Frisco ISD program that pairs students with a mentor in their field of interest for a
			year of original research and product development. Alongside a research portfolio of
			observations, interviews, and professional contacts, the program pushes you to build real
			goal-setting, communication, and public speaking skills, ending in a formal presentation of
			your original work.
		</p>
		<p>
			My ISM research is on <strong>photodynamic therapy (PDT)</strong>, light-activated cancer
			treatment, under Dr. Vanderlei Bagnato at Texas A&#38;M. That research became a 14-page
			manuscript, presented at the UNT Frisco ISM Showcase and currently pending publication, plus a
			handful of AI tools that grew out of it. You can read about those on the{" "}
			<a href="/projects/">projects page</a>, and follow the week-by-week process on the{" "}
			<a href="/posts/">journal</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Mentor: Dr. Vanderlei Salvador Bagnato</h2>
		<p>
			Dr. Bagnato is a professor of physics at Texas A&#38;M University and a pioneer in biophotonics
			and photodynamic therapy, with a joint appointment at the University of São Paulo. He’s
			published 500+ peer-reviewed papers over a 40-year research career, and his work on PDT
			dosimetry has directly shaped clinical protocols used in cancer therapy today. He’s been
			generous enough to mentor my research into that work over the past year.
		</p>

		<h2>Skills</h2>
		<p>Python · PyTorch · React · FastAPI · Pandas · Machine Learning · CNNs · NLP · OCR</p>

